  "noise": "Independent Gaussian innovations with variance 1; continuous stationary AR noise within each run, independent run restarts after 256 burn-in draws. Censoring only affects estimator/whitener layout, not the data generator.",
  "design": "Two alternating 4-second task epochs at onsets 6+32k, sampled at TR=1 and convolved with public SPMG1; run intercepts and six run-local DCT nuisance terms per run in high-nuisance cells.",
  "censor_rule": "Within each run censor rows 23,24,60 and then every 37 rows beginning at 97 when in range; reset on the following row; censored response rows remain on the fitting axis.",
  "truth": "Voxel 0 task coefficients are both 0; voxel 1 task_a is 0.75, task_b is -0.25; nuisance and intercept coefficients fixed; independent replicate datasets are the sampling units.",
  "pairing": "One independent innovation sequence per replicate is reused across all 24 diagnostic cells; differences in AR order filter the same innovations. Pooling, nuisance and censor comparisons are paired. Each cell has 512 independent replicates; there are 512 independent diagnostic innovation blocks, not 12288 independent experiments. Short confirmation pooling cells share 2048 fresh blocks; long confirmation has a separate 2048-block stream.",
  "diagnostic_endpoints": [
    "all original measurement endpoints",
    "reported variance / empirical estimator variance decomposition against known-phi",
    "mean variance scale, normalized task-a covariance geometry and their covariance",
    "paired factor main effects and conditional effects with dataset-bootstrap 90% intervals",
    "AR coefficient MSE per run/voxel rather than averaging coefficient accuracy across voxels"
  ],
  "diagnostic_decision": "Diagnostic data identify measured factor effects and variance decomposition; they confer no scientific admission. Do not ascribe cause when paired effects or variance decomposition do not support it. Confirmation evaluates all three predeclared existing-configuration mitigations independently against original frozen margins, regardless of diagnostic outcome. Retain every failure. No nominal-df replacement or production estimator/inference change is declared.",
  "scope_limits": [
    "No group/PM/mKH qualification or resumption of historical/spent calibration campaigns",
    "No effective-df implementation or blanket FGLS-variance-independence claim",
    "No corrected iterative/robust fit or ARMA estimation",
    "No scientific admission from screen or pilot results",
    "Known-phi censor-reset whitening is a known-parameter comparator, not an exact inverse of the continuous-noise covariance; its calibration is measured rather than presumed.",
    "Homogeneous AR truth across four independent response columns; pooling recommendations do not apply to heterogeneous noise.",
    "Long-run confirmation doubles run duration while keeping six DCT terms per run and extending the same task/censor rule; this is a configuration mitigation, not isolated identification of a pure sample-size effect.",
    "Original short-run voxelwise failure remains binding; no broad corrected-GLS admission."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/Binomial.html"
  ]
